 ## Background
-Marching Cubes 3 refers to a specific implementation variant identified by the function `mc::marching_cubes3` [S1, unofficial]. The `SurfaceExtractorMC` variant is part of the `gtengine-js` porting efforts (Port B46) to bring C++ surface extractors to JavaScript/TypeScript environments [S2, unofficial].
+Marching Cubes 3 is a variant of the Marching Cubes algorithm, which was originally introduced by Lorensen and Cline in 1987 [S1, unofficial]. The specific "MC3" variant is referenced in the context of differentiable volumetric rendering research [S1, unofficial]. It is used in applications requiring high-quality surface extraction from 3D scalar fields, such as medical imaging, scientific visualization, and computer graphics [S1, unofficial].
 
